<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="62c015bc">&lt;p&gt;
    Prepare for a project kickoff meeting by developing the necessary documents highlighting the project scope, schedule,
    cost, risks, and communication plan for discussion with project team.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Prepare the kickoff materials.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop&amp;nbsp;kickoff materials based on the requirements of the project or program team and support
        organization.&amp;nbsp; These materials should include an overview of the project plan and a review of the procedures.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ask the sponsor of the project or program to prepare&amp;nbsp;materials.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ask the sponsor to develop an overview of the methodology and a business background summary.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Compile all of the obtained&amp;nbsp;kickoff&amp;nbsp;materials.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="15668c8a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="3f6f6888">&lt;p&gt;
    When developing and executing communications and events, keep the following in mind:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        In collaboration with the correct team (e.g., Solution Design Team, Technical Team, etc.), design and develop the
        communications collateral
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop and maintain a communication tracker in order to identify the key messages, timing, delivery channel(s),
        frequency, owners and feedback mechanisms for each communication and event
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        For each type of stakeholder group, execute targeted communications and events (as required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Maintain the communications tracker for the life of the program. Continually update the tracker against
        communication feedback received to meet the changing needs of the program and its stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="3cb5be2c"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="9a73e1ac">To verify that the project kickoff presentation and supporting information is aligned with, and appropriate for, the client
audience.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="eda10a40"></attribute>
